export default "Cervical and breast results can arrive as a portal note, a letter, or a call. The words can be short and hard to hold in your head.\n\nThis page keeps the work small. Copy the words. Write your questions. Do not use this page to explain, interpret, or diagnose a result.\n\nAsk your clinician or imaging center what your own result means.\n\n## Pick your result type\n\n| Result type | Jump to |\n|---|---|\n| Abnormal Pap result | [Abnormal Pap result notes](#abnormal-pap-result-notes) |\n| HPV-positive Pap result | [HPV-positive Pap notes](#hpv-positive-pap-notes) |\n| Pap smear terms you do not understand | [Pap smear terms card](#pap-smear-terms-card) |\n| Colposcopy visit, before results | [Colposcopy question checklist](#colposcopy-question-checklist) |\n| Colposcopy or biopsy recovery | [Colposcopy recovery notes](#colposcopy-recovery-notes) |\n| Cervical biopsy result | [Cervical biopsy result notes](#cervical-biopsy-result-notes) |\n| Mammogram result | [Mammogram result notes](#mammogram-result-notes) |\n| Abnormal mammogram result | [Abnormal mammogram result notes](#abnormal-mammogram-result-notes) |\n| Breast ultrasound result | [Breast ultrasound result notes](#breast-ultrasound-result-notes) |\n| Breast biopsy result | [Breast biopsy result notes](#breast-biopsy-result-notes) |\n| Breast lump before a period | [Breast lump cycle notes](#breast-lump-cycle-notes) |\n| Breast cyst symptoms | [Breast cyst symptom notes](#breast-cyst-symptom-notes) |\n\n## Abnormal Pap result notes\n\nCopy the words exactly as shown. Do not rewrite them yet.\n\n| Item | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Test date | |\n| Report date | |\n| Clinic or lab name | |\n| Exact Pap result words | |\n| HPV status, if shown | positive / negative / not shown |\n| HPV type, if shown | |\n| Result note from portal | |\n| Clinician message | |\n| Prior screening date | |\n| Prior colposcopy, if any | |\n\nCDC explains that a Pap test checks cervical cells and an HPV test checks cells for HPV. NCI explains that abnormal HPV and Pap results need clinician review, with terms like ASC-US, LSIL, HSIL, unsatisfactory, and HPV-positive. ACOG explains cervical cancer screening may use a Pap test, an HPV test, or both.\n\nAsk: What are the exact result words? Was an HPV test done too? Do you need my last Pap or HPV date? Is the full lab report in the portal?\n\nHHS says people have rights to see and get copies of health records from covered providers and health plans.\n\n## HPV-positive Pap notes\n\nKeep the Pap line and HPV line separate. Do not turn the words into a meaning on your own.\n\n| Item | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Test date | |\n| HPV result line | |\n| HPV type, if shown | |\n| Pap result line | |\n| Lab note | |\n| Prior screening date | |\n| Main question | |\n\nNCI explains HPV and Pap test result terms and says clinicians may use HPV and Pap results together when reviewing cervical screening. ACOG explains that HPV testing may be done with Pap testing or after a Pap test result.\n\nAsk: Which line is the Pap result? Which line is the HPV result? Was HPV typed or genotyped? Can you explain this in plain words?\n\nKeep this note focused on lab words and questions. Leave out partner names, personal guesses about why HPV was found, and care plans.\n\n## Pap smear terms card\n\nUse this if your report has a short term you do not recognize.\n\n| Term on report | Did I see it? | Question to ask |\n|---|---|---|\n| NILM | yes / no / not sure | What does NILM mean here? |\n| ASC-US | yes / no / not sure | What does ASC-US mean here? |\n| LSIL | yes / no / not sure | What does LSIL mean here? |\n| HSIL | yes / no / not sure | What does HSIL mean here? |\n| HPV | yes / no / not sure | Was HPV found or not found? |\n| Unsatisfactory | yes / no / not sure | What made the sample unsatisfactory? |\n| Colposcopy | yes / no / not sure | Why is this word listed? |\n\nNCI describes cervical screening result terms including ASC-US, LSIL, HSIL, unsatisfactory results, HPV-positive results, and colposcopy. Copy the exact term. Do not change the letters. Ask your clinician to say it in plain words.\n\n## Colposcopy question checklist\n\nUse this before a colposcopy visit. It does not tell you how to prepare your body. Follow your clinic's own instructions.\n\n| Prompt | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Date of screening test | |\n| Pap wording | |\n| HPV wording | |\n| Portal message wording | |\n| Why the clinic said to come in | |\n| Main question I have | |\n\nNCI says colposcopy may be used after some abnormal HPV or Pap results, with biopsy samples checked under a microscope. ACOG explains that colposcopy provides more information after abnormal screening results and can involve biopsy.\n\nAsk: Why was colposcopy recommended for me? Will a biopsy be discussed? If a biopsy is done, when might results appear? What will show in my portal?\n\n## Colposcopy recovery notes\n\nUse this after a colposcopy or cervical biopsy. This is a note sheet, not a care plan. It does not give a recovery time, aftercare steps, sex timing rules, tampon rules, or activity rules. Follow the instructions from your clinic.\n\n| Instruction topic | What my clinic said |\n|---|---|\n| Bleeding or discharge notes | |\n| Medicine notes | |\n| Activity notes | |\n| Sex or tampon notes | |\n| When to call | |\n| Result follow-up | |\n\nNCI says bleeding, discharge, or cramp-like pain may occur after biopsy, and your clinic should tell you what to expect in your case.\n\n| Date and time | What I noticed | Amount | Color or texture | Question |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | | | | |\n\nAsk: Was a biopsy done? Where will results appear? What symptoms should make me call?\n\n## Cervical biopsy result notes\n\nCopy the words. Your clinician should explain what the result means for you.\n\n| Field | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Biopsy date | |\n| Result posted date | |\n| Exact result wording | |\n| Portal message wording | |\n| Follow-up date, if listed | |\n| Main question | |\n\n| Word on report | Exact wording | Question for clinician |\n|---|---|---|\n| CIN | | What does this mean in my result? |\n| Grade | | Is this the grade on my report? |\n| LSIL | | Is this screening wording or biopsy wording here? |\n| HSIL | | Is this screening wording or biopsy wording here? |\n| Margins | | Does this word matter in my report? |\n| Follow-up | | What is the next step and why? |\n\nNCI explains that cervical biopsy samples are checked by a pathologist, and that biopsy reports may use CIN wording for abnormal cervical cells found on the cervix surface. CDC says clinicians decide how best to follow up on abnormal cervical screening results.\n\n## Mammogram result notes\n\nCopy the words first. Ask your clinic to explain them.\n\n| Field | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Mammogram date | |\n| Report date | |\n| Exact result words | |\n| Breast density wording, if shown | |\n| Portal note or letter words | |\n| Main question | |\n\nNCI explains that mammograms are x-ray images of the breasts, used for screening or diagnostic evaluation. NCI says dense breasts are a common mammogram finding. ACR says mammogram result summaries should use plain language.\n\nAsk: Where can I see the full report? Does the report include breast density wording? Can I get a copy of the images?\n\n## Abnormal mammogram result notes\n\nCopy what you see. Do not use this page to explain the result.\n\n| Field | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Mammogram date | |\n| Report date | |\n| Exact result words | |\n| Portal message or letter words | |\n| Who called or wrote | |\n| Main question | |\n\n| Question | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Last mammogram date | |\n| Prior imaging center | |\n| Prior ultrasound, if any | |\n| Where old reports are saved | |\n\nAmerican Cancer Society says a callback may involve more mammograms or another test, such as ultrasound, so the clinic can look more closely at an area.\n\nAsk: Can you explain the exact result words? Is this note a summary or the full report? Do you need older mammogram images or reports?\n\n## Breast ultrasound result notes\n\nCopy the exact words. This page does not read ultrasound images or explain result categories.\n\n| Field | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Ultrasound date | |\n| Report date | |\n| Exact result words | |\n| Portal message or letter words | |\n| Mammogram date, if linked | |\n| Main question | |\n\nNCI explains that diagnostic mammograms may be used to check for breast cancer after a woman or her doctor finds a lump or other change. American Cancer Society explains that after a mammogram callback, more mammograms or other tests, such as ultrasound, may be used to look more closely at an area.\n\nAsk: Was this ultrasound linked to a mammogram? Which words should I copy for my own record?\n\n## Breast biopsy result notes\n\nCopy the words first. Do not try to decode them here.\n\n| Field | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Biopsy date | |\n| Result posted date | |\n| Exact report wording | |\n| Portal message wording | |\n| Main question | |\n\n| Word on report | Exact wording | Question for clinician |\n|---|---|---|\n| Pathology | | Who can explain this report? |\n| Benign | | What does this word mean in my result? |\n| Atypia | | Does this word appear in my report? |\n| Calcifications | | Is this imaging wording or biopsy wording here? |\n| Margins | | Does this word matter in my report? |\n| Pending | | Is any result still pending? |\n\nNCI says breast biopsy results come in a lab report. American Cancer Society explains breast biopsy report words.\n\nAsk: What is the exact result? Which part of the report matters most? Who wrote the lab report?\n\n## Breast lump cycle notes\n\nA breast lump before a period can be hard to explain. This sheet does not tell you the cause, and it does not say the lump is from hormones or is harmless.\n\n| Question | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Date noticed | |\n| Last period start date | |\n| Days before expected period | |\n| Left, right, or both | |\n| Location words | |\n| Your words for the change | |\n| Pain or tenderness | no / yes |\n| Skin or nipple change | no / yes |\n| Prior note or visit about this | no / yes / not sure |\n\nMayo Clinic says cyclic breast pain is related to the menstrual cycle and may come with swelling, fullness, or lumpiness. Mayo Clinic lists breast cyst symptoms that can include a movable lump, nipple discharge, and size or tenderness changes around a period. Cleveland Clinic says a clinical breast exam may be used for breast changes such as pain, skin changes, nipple fluid, or lumps.\n\nUse words you would say out loud. \"Left outer side, pea-sized spot\" is enough. Do not force a reason into the notes.\n\n## Breast cyst symptom notes\n\nThis is a question list, not a diagnostic checklist. Do not use it to decide if a breast change is a cyst.\n\n| Question | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Date noticed | |\n| Left, right, or both | |\n| Location words | |\n| Pain or tenderness | no / yes |\n| Nipple fluid noticed | no / yes |\n| Last period start date | |\n| Did it change near bleeding? | no / yes / not sure |\n| Prior imaging or visit | no / yes / not sure |\n| Main question | |\n\nMayo Clinic lists breast cyst symptoms that can include a movable lump, nipple discharge, pain or tenderness near the lump, and size or tenderness changes around a period. Mayo Clinic says evaluation for a breast cyst may include a breast exam, imaging, or fine-needle aspiration. NCI lists breast conditions that may involve lumps, pain, nipple discharge, or symptoms around the menstrual period. Cleveland Clinic says follow-up tests after an abnormal clinical breast exam may include mammogram, ultrasound, breast MRI, or biopsy.\n\nThis list does not rank danger and does not decide whether a change is a cyst, harmless, or cancer. Those are clinician questions.\n\n## Records and portal access\n\nHHS says people have rights to see and get copies of health records from covered providers and health plans, including asking for corrections.\n\nAsk your clinic or imaging center:\n\n- Can I download the full report?\n- Can I get the images too?\n- Who can see this portal result?\n- Does proxy access affect this result?\n- Can I correct a wrong name, date, or phone number?\n\n## Privacy note\n\nCervical and breast result notes can include sex history, HPV status, images, clinic names, insurance, family history, and portal messages.\n\nKeep the smallest useful note.\n\n| Instead of saving | Try saving |\n|---|---|\n| Full portal screenshot | Exact result words |\n| Full phone transcript | Main question |\n| Full image file | Where images are stored |\n| Full app export | Short clinic note |\n\nFTC guidance says health information can include more than diagnoses and treatment. Small details, such as browsing or location data, can still imply health facts.\n\n## Floriva note\n\nFloriva can hold short notes on your device. It cannot control clinics, labs, portals, email, insurance, screenshots, backups, or shared devices.\n\nFor less saved detail, read the [lab results privacy checklist](/resources/privacy-in-practice/your-medical-records-and-period-data) and the [patient portal privacy checklist](/resources/privacy-in-practice/your-medical-records-and-period-data). For broader visit prep, use [Floriva for gynecologist prep](/app-guides/floriva-for-gynecologist-prep) and the [reproductive health visit prep kit](/free/reproductive-visit-prep-kit).";
